OL,3,GNEWSAContinuing rise in home-schooling
OL,4,Abeing 'monitored'
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe number of children being schooled
OL,7,Fat home is continuing to rise in
OL,8,FBlackpool, new figures have indicated.
OL,10,FThe town's council said it was
OL,11,F"monitoring" the changes, which have
OL,12,Fseen the number increase from just over
OL,13,F600 in 2024 to more than 750 in July
OL,14,Fthis year.
OL,16,FChildren becoming "less visible" to the
OL,17,Flocal authority was said by Blackpool
OL,18,FCouncil to be one of the main risks of
OL,19,Fthe rise.
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
